"""Minnesota state content: lessons and practice questions.

Minnesota splits the salesperson examination and sets ONE pass mark that
applies to each portion separately. The PSI Minnesota Real Estate Candidate
Information Bulletin, examination summary table: Salesperson General 80
items / 2.5 hours; State 50 items / 1.5 hours; both 130 items / 4 hours.
Minn. Stat. 82.59 subd. 6 sets the mark: "a score of 75 percent or higher
on the uniform portion and a score of 75 percent or higher on the state
portion."

Minnesota's agency law is its own animal. The statute sets out FOUR
relationships on a mandatory disclosure form - SELLER'S BROKER, BUYER'S
BROKER, DUAL AGENT and FACILITATOR - and until a consumer signs a written
representation contract they are a CUSTOMER, not a client, and the licensee
is a FACILITATOR by default. A facilitator owes NO fiduciary duty EXCEPT
CONFIDENTIALITY. Dual agency is permitted with informed written consent,
and a dual agent may not advocate for either party.

Note on the weights below. PSI publishes the Minnesota state outline with
item counts that total 40 (Brokerage License Law 20, Interests in Real
Property 8, Conveyance Procedures 8, Financial Instruments 4), while the
examination summary table in the same bulletin gives the state portion 50
items. The published counts are not exhaustive. This pack keeps PSI's
published proportions and scales them to the 50 items the table actually
sets - x1.25, so 20/8/8/4 becomes 25/10/10/5 - then splits the 25-item
license-law block into the subtopics the outline itself names.

Every rule below was read on 2026-11-11 from the official text:
  - Minn. Stat. chapter 82 (Real Estate Brokers and Salespersons), from
    revisor.mn.gov - in particular 82.59, 82.61, 82.62, 82.63, 82.66,
    82.67, 82.68, 82.69, 82.70, 82.71, 82.72, 82.73, 82.735, 82.74,
    82.75, 82.81, 82.82, 82.83, 82.85 and 82.86.
  - Minn. Stat. 507.02 (conveyances by spouses), 513.54 to 513.60 (seller
    disclosure), 103I.235 (well disclosure), 115.55 subd. 6 (subsurface
    sewage disclosure), 327A.02 (statutory warranties), 363A.09 (Human
    Rights Act, real property), 287.035 and 287.21 (mortgage registry and
    deed tax), 580.23 (redemption), 559.21 (contract for deed
    cancellation), 515B.4-107 (resale of units) and 504B.178 (security
    deposits), all from revisor.mn.gov.
  - The PSI Minnesota Real Estate Candidate Information Bulletin, published
    at test-takers.psiexams.com/mnre, for the examination table, the
    licence requirements and the state content outline.
The section a fact comes from is cited next to it. Do not add a fact here
without reading its source first.
"""

