    ("mn/conduct", "Records", 3, "Which need NOT be retained?", "An agency disclosure form where no contractual relationship followed and no services were provided", ["A cancelled trust account check", "An executed purchase agreement"], "82.72 subd. 3(1)"),
    ("mn/conduct", "Records", 2, "Minnesota broker record storage may be:", "Electronic", ["Paper only", "Off-site only with Commissioner approval"], "82.72 subd. 4"),
    ("mn/conduct", "Records", 3, "After the retention period, documents must be disposed of according to:", "The confidential record destruction procedures of the Fair and Accurate Credit Transaction Act of 2003", ["Any reasonable method", "The Commissioner's written instructions"], "82.72 subd. 5"),
    ("mn/conduct", "Supervision", 2, "A Minnesota broker's supervision duty includes:", "Ongoing monitoring of transaction documents and review of all trust account books and records", ["Monthly office meetings", "Annual licensee evaluations"], "82.73 subd. 3(a)"),
    ("mn/conduct", "Supervision", 2, "Designating another broker to supervise a place of business:", "Does not relieve the primary broker of ultimate responsibility", ["Transfers all responsibility", "Requires Commissioner approval"], "82.73 subd. 3(a)"),
    ("mn/conduct", "Supervision", 2, "A broker's file of written complaints about each licensee must be kept for:", "Three years", ["One year", "Six years", "Permanently"], "82.73 subd. 3(c)"),
    ("mn/conduct", "Supervision", 3, "An unlicensed assistant may disclose:", "Factual information about the broker's listings, if the broker provided it in written form", ["Nothing at all", "Price opinions", "Anything the assistant knows"], "82.73 subd. 3(d)"),
    ("mn/conduct", "Supervision", 3, "Every real estate office must keep available a current copy of:", "Chapter 82, chapter 83 and the rules adopted under them", ["Chapter 82 only", "The NAR Code of Ethics"], "82.73 subd. 1"),
    ("mn/conduct", "Prohibitions", 3, "A purchase agreement may contain an arbitration clause covering a licensee's liability only if:", "The licensee is a principal in the transaction", ["Both parties initial it", "The broker signs it separately"], "82.81 subd. 5"),
    ("mn/conduct", "Prohibitions", 2, "In a residential closing, a licensee may not:", "Require a person to use a particular lender, attorney, closing agent or title insurance agent", ["Recommend a title company", "Provide a list of lenders"], "82.81 subd. 8"),
    ("mn/conduct", "Prohibitions", 2, "Discouraging a party from seeking the services of an attorney is:", "Prohibited", ["Permitted to speed the closing", "Permitted if the broker is experienced"], "82.81 subd. 11"),
    ("mn/conduct", "Prohibitions", 3, "A licensee may discuss a post-expiration listing with an owner under an exclusive contract if:", "The owner initiates the discussion and the licensee asks whether such a contract exists", ["The listing expires within 30 days", "The other broker is notified"], "82.81 subd. 9(c)"),
    ("mn/conduct", "Prohibitions", 2, "Inducing a party to breach an exclusive listing or buyer's agreement is:", "Prohibited", ["Permitted if better for the client", "Permitted after 30 days"], "82.81 subd. 9(b)"),
    ("mn/conduct", "Prohibitions", 3, "When the SELLER cannot close through no fault of the buyer, the listing broker:", "May not claim any portion of the buyer's trust funds absent a separate agreement with the buyer", ["May deduct the commission", "May split the deposit with the seller"], "82.81 subd. 3"),
    ("mn/conduct", "Prohibitions", 2, "Which is a statutory fraudulent, deceptive or dishonest practice?", "Demanding a commission from a seller knowing the licensee is not entitled to it", ["Charging an above-market commission", "Declining a listing"], "82.81 subd. 12(a)(13)"),
    ("mn/conduct", "Prohibitions", 3, "A final court decision that a licensee violated Minnesota's antitrust sections means:", "The licensee is deemed to have violated 82.81", ["Nothing for licensing purposes", "A separate hearing on the merits is required"], "82.81 subd. 12(b)"),
    ("mn/conduct", "Prohibitions", 3, "A chapter 82 licence does not authorise:", "Dealing in vendor's interests in contracts for deed or mortgagee's interests in mortgages, beyond the limited exception", ["Leasing residential property", "Selling business opportunities"], "82.81 subd. 7"),
    ("mn/conduct", "Discipline", 1, "A violation of Minnesota's real estate chapter is a:", "Gross misdemeanor", ["Petty misdemeanor", "Felony", "Civil infraction"], "82.83"),
    ("mn/conduct", "Discipline", 2, "After a summary suspension, a hearing on the merits must be held within:", "30 days of the suspension order", ["10 days", "60 days", "90 days"], "82.82 subd. 5"),
    ("mn/conduct", "Discipline", 2, "Failing to reasonably supervise is a ground for discipline when it:", "Causes injury or harm to the public", ["Is merely negligent", "Involves more than five licensees"], "82.82 subd. 1(d)"),
    ("mn/conduct", "Discipline", 3, "May the Commissioner press a licensee into a monetary settlement with a consumer?", "No; the Commissioner shall not coerce or attempt to coerce one", ["Yes, during any investigation", "Yes, if the consumer asks"], "82.82 subd. 4"),
    ("mn/conduct", "Discipline", 3, "The Commissioner's order to show cause must:", "State the specific statute or rule violated", ["Include a proposed penalty", "Be served by the sheriff"], "82.82 subd. 5"),
    ("mn/conduct", "Discipline", 2, "The sanctions available to the Commissioner are:", "Denial, suspension, revocation or censure", ["A fine of up to $5,000 only", "Criminal prosecution only"], "82.82 subd. 1"),
